        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Figure 5. HERA single-epoch rank sweep and Pareto proxy diagnostics. (a) Residual-contamination proxy (blue, lower is better) decreases with increasing rank while science-distortion proxy (orange, lower is better) increases. The shaded region indicates the non-identifiable rank range (approximately  $ k = 5-20 $) where both errors remain high. (b) Pareto projection of the same proxies (colored by rank). The front exhibits a clear knee and non-zero error floor, showing that no single rank simultaneously minimizes residual contamination and distortion. Compare with the synthetic Pareto panels in Figure 4.</div>\n",
            "block_bbox": [
